<!--
  Primitives: the raw values Motif's look is built from, named by value and carrying no meaning.

  Nothing outside Intent.axaml names a key here. A view or a component style that wants a colour, a gap or a
  size asks Intent for what it means; Intent picks the primitive. A primitive is theme-invariant: a colour
  that differs between light and dark is two primitives, and Intent's theme dictionaries choose between them.

  Where Semi.Avalonia's own scale holds the same value, the primitive aliases Semi's key, so the two
  scales cannot drift apart. Semi's colour ramp is not aliased: its light and dark palettes give one key
  two values, and a primitive has one.

  Key shapes: Primitive.Color.<Hue><Step>, Primitive.Space.<px>, Primitive.Inset.<left>_<top>_<right>_<bottom>,
  Primitive.Radius.<px>, Primitive.Type.<px>, Primitive.Size.<px>, Primitive.Stroke.<px>, Primitive.Dash.<on>_<off>, Primitive.Opacity.<percent>, Primitive.Font.<family>.
  A decimal point in a value is written as p (13p5 is 13.5).
-->
<ResourceDictionary xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
                    xmlns:collections="clr-namespace:Avalonia.Collections;assembly=Avalonia.Base">

